Validate the buffer's length fields before calling helpers that subtract them.
Keep the network-header offset signed: a negative value may name bytes in headroom.
Reject INT_MIN before negation, then prove the magnitude fits in skb_headroom().
For a nonnegative offset, prove it is no larger than skb->len.
Validate the requested network-relative range by checking before subtracting.
Add that offset to the signed skb offset in s64, then prove the result fits int.
Only after geometry and fragment readability are known should you call
skb_header_pointer_careful() and commit local output values.
